1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,054
Meet Dark Ops, by Sherlops: an operations intelligence prototype for quick commerce stores.

2
00:00:06,054 --> 00:00:10,962
This is the working application, running locally with synthetic Bengaluru data.

3
00:00:10,962 --> 00:00:21,151
The dashboard brings together identified loss, open investigations, waste rate, and stock approaching expiry, so a store lead can decide where to investigate first.

4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:23,967
Let's focus on Indiranagar.

5
00:00:23,967 --> 00:00:29,479
Changing the store filter updates the operational snapshot and narrows the investigation queue.

6
00:00:29,479 --> 00:00:32,381
Returning to all stores restores the network view.

7
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:36,384
The main metrics are calculated by the backend from the demo records.

8
00:00:36,384 --> 00:00:40,562
Some surrounding comparison labels remain illustrative prototype values.

9
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,644
Next, we open Investigations and search for tomatoes.

10
00:00:45,644 --> 00:00:47,481
The queue narrows immediately.

11
00:00:47,481 --> 00:00:53,540
Opening the matching case reveals the affected product, store, estimated loss, and complaint photo.

12
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:59,172
The case keeps the operational signal and its supporting context together, ready for review.

13
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:05,264
Scrolling through the case reveals why it was flagged and the supporting measurements.

14
00:01:05,264 --> 00:01:12,957
The tomato waste spike is compared with its baseline, while other evidence helps distinguish a supplier problem from a change in demand.

15
00:01:12,957 --> 00:01:15,502
Ranked hypotheses make the reasoning visible.

16
00:01:15,502 --> 00:01:19,292
These rankings are prototype signals, not calibrated probabilities.

17
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,052
Now we request a live Gemini investigation.

18
00:01:27,052 --> 00:01:31,306
Dark Ops sends the case's synthetic evidence to the configured model.

19
00:01:31,306 --> 00:01:37,164
The returned report explains a likely cause, proposes next steps, and identifies evidence gaps.

20
00:01:37,164 --> 00:01:41,111
The operator can compare that explanation with the measurements.

21
00:01:41,111 --> 00:01:46,106
Gemini interprets the supplied facts; it does not calculate the dashboard totals.

22
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,434
We record the suggested action for the store manager.

23
00:01:53,434 --> 00:01:57,155
The application confirms the action and attaches it to this case.

24
00:01:57,155 --> 00:02:03,108
This is a simulated workflow record: it does not send a supplier claim or change a retailer's inventory.

25
00:02:03,108 --> 00:02:05,913
Recording the action unlocks the follow-up check.

26
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:15,862
Clicking Simulate plus seven days completes the follow-up and displays the before-and-after values.

27
00:02:15,862 --> 00:02:19,227
The case now has a recorded action and a verification result.

28
00:02:19,227 --> 00:02:25,793
These outcomes are synthetic, demonstrating how the workflow closes the loop without claiming a real-world improvement.

29
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,649
The Photo Forensics Lab adds another evidence path.

30
00:02:31,649 --> 00:02:36,810
We analyze an AI-generated tomato complaint photo using live Gemini on Vertex AI.

31
00:02:36,810 --> 00:02:42,353
The result shows visible damage, an assessment, confidence, and a recommended response.

32
00:02:42,353 --> 00:02:45,220
Package details can be reported when legible.

33
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:51,783
The engine label identifies the analysis used, and a human can review the recommendation before acting.

34
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,375
Now we select the seeded duplicate-photo complaint.

35
00:02:59,375 --> 00:03:05,150
The application compares a perceptual hash with its local image index and flags a match for review.

36
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:10,049
Although the interface uses the word vector, this prototype uses perceptual hashing.

37
00:03:10,049 --> 00:03:14,658
A matching photo is a review signal, not proof that a customer committed fraud.

38
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:21,316
Finally, we export the investigation report.

39
00:03:21,316 --> 00:03:27,546
Dark Ops connects signals, evidence, analysis, action, and follow-up in one working prototype.

40
00:03:27,546 --> 00:03:28,606
Find the signal.

41
00:03:28,606 --> 00:03:29,600
Build the case.
